========================================================================
3e) Workflow shape (cdk-app-update) — 3 agent stages
========================================================================

```
clone → clone-blocked-gate → implement-cdk → validate → validate-loop-gate ↺ implement-cdk
```

**Validate stage** runs CDK checks on the branch already pushed in **edit**. **Edit stage** opens the draft PR.

| Stage | Owns (write) |
|-------|----------------|
| `clone` | trigger fields, `issue_details`, `repo_clone_path`, `repo_head_sha`, `gate_result` |
| `implement-cdk` | `module_paths`, `implement_*`, `working_branch`, `pr_url`, `pr_title`, `pr_draft` |
| `validate` | `validation_summary`, `test_summary_tail`, `module_quality_gaps`, `quality_check_*`, `module_quality_summary` |

**Stage-boundary spawn rules (hard):**
| Stage | Allowed runners | Forbidden |
|-------|-----------------|-----------|
| `clone` | `clone-runner`, `clone-fetch`, `progress-comment-updater` | `implement-cdk-*`, `validate-runner`, `create-pr-*`, `load_skill` |
| `implement-cdk` | `implement-cdk-resolve-paths`, `implement-cdk-app-update`, `implement-cdk-catalog-scaffold`, `create-pr-runner`, `progress-comment-updater` | `validate-runner`, `create-pr-notify`, `load_skill` |
| `validate` | `validate-runner`, `create-pr-notify`, `create-pr-comment`, `progress-comment-updater` | `create-pr-runner`, `implement-cdk-*`, `load_skill` |

========================================================================
3d) Execution Optimization Protocol — batch remote runner calls
========================================================================

**Hard rule.** Use **ONE** `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_series` per shell subagent with spawn-context one-liners.

| Situation | Tool |
|-----------|------|
| One command | `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_command` |
| Ordered multi-step (clone, validate, commit+push) | **`${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_series`** |
| Shell-heavy stage work | ONE series with pack ensure + `stage-runner.sh` / `clone-pack.sh` |

**Shell `$`:** single `$` only — never `$$` (PID expansion breaks pack decode).

**Subagent spawn discipline:**
- Approved names from spawn contracts only — never invent recovery subagents.
- `task_type="terminal_calling"` for shell-heavy subagents.
- Planner iteration budget: **40** — batch notes per §3i.

========================================================================
3f) Evidence gate (`validate` stage)
========================================================================

Before declaring workflow success, verify `submit_evidence` for required items on **`cdk-bot-module-update-evidence`**. Do **not** post "✅ Compliant" when `module_quality_summary` is not `PASS` or any `stage_summary:*` is `blocked:`.

========================================================================
3j) Live progress issue comment (Template P)
========================================================================

When `enable_progress_issue_comment=true`, each agent stage ends with ONE `progress-comment-updater` subagent.

| Mark | After stage completes |
|------|------------------------|
| `PROGRESS_clone` | `clone`: `done` when `repo_clone_path` set |
| `PROGRESS_implement` | `implement-cdk`: `done` when `pr_url` or `implement_edit_verified=true` |
| `PROGRESS_validate` | `validate`: `done` when `module_quality_summary` is PASS/NEEDS_REVISION/BLOCKED |

========================================================================
3g) When `ask_clarifying_question` is appropriate
========================================================================

Use for: missing PAT, ambiguous `module_paths` when issue body lacks file hints. **Never** for CDK edits when `issue_details.body` names files — re-spawn `implement-cdk-app-update`.

========================================================================
3h) Workflow script pack — single-command embed
========================================================================

Load **`${module_prefix}-workflow-script-pack`** before spawning script runners (planner only — embedded runners must **not** `load_skill`).

1. `WORK_ROOT` from spawn context — absolute path under remote runner home.
2. Each runner: **ONE** `execute_series` with spawn-context Clone / Validate / Commit-pr / Discovery command.
3. **Discovery greenfield:** inline validate in catalog-scaffold series when enabled; validate stage may skip duplicate runner when `catalog_greenfield_validated=true` and PASS.
